      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T13:45:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the automotive software, Xen is widely used as type-1 hypervisor.  For example, the SOAFEE [1] defines the standard for automotive software in the community and EWAOL is an implementation for the standard [2] which deploys Xen virtulisation.\n\nThough I have no concrete performance data, I think a main reason for using Xen virtulisation is because it can give lower latency rather than other KVM.  And the low latency and realtime performance is critical for automotive software.\n\nHere I am not quite agree that Xen is \"legacy virtualization\", if you look at Xen mailing list [3], you could see Xen is an active project.  And as I know, there have many ongoing development for it (e.g. support virtio devices for Xen).\n\n[1] https://www.soafee.io/\n[2] https://ewaol.docs.arm.com/en/kirkstone-dev/introduction.html#high-level-overview\n[3] https://lore.kernel.org/xen-devel/",
      "parentUuid": "fdb02333_416bf820",
      "revId": "61214567014ac28d87c837ec69cae43134d90f42",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3fd4f9ec_e2ce10a2",
