      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T18:18:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know the project is \"active\", but it really is only going into \"legacy\" products, like automotive 😊\n\nAlso, KVM can do real-time, if you really want that (note realtime does not mean lower latency at all, it means deterministic latency.)\n\nIf this is enabled, it opens up a whole new part of the kernel that needs to be maintained and made stable for abi issues for a release.  It also introduces a whole new attack surface.  And it needs a maintainer to be able to manage it all over the next 5-10 years.\n\nSo, as with all new kernel features that want to be added, please fill out the proper documentation for it (there\u0027s a web form somewhere), and also get the security team to buy into this, as they will also need to be aware that they will now need to audit, and track, all future Xen issues when it comes to Android kernels.",
      "parentUuid": "3fd4f9ec_e2ce10a2",
      "revId": "61214567014ac28d87c837ec69cae43134d90f42",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
